sentences.say:
La beauté, pour le sexe, est un rare trésor ;
De l’admirer jamais on ne se lasse ;
Mais ce qu’on nomme bonne grâce,
Est sans prix, et vaut mieux encor.

sentences.l:
Beauty, for the sex, is a rare treasure;
Of admiring it never does one tire;
But what one names good grace
Is without price, and is worth more still.

sentences.i:
In women, beauty is a rare treasure;
no one ever wearies of admiring it;
but what is called graciousness
is beyond price, and worth more still.

Fair ladies, this gift is worth more than a well-dressed head;
to win a heart and carry the day,
graciousness is the true gift of the fairies;
without it you can do nothing, with it you can do all.
